			<div class="content" id="post-content-2338518">
									

<p>To be fair, though, it doesn't cover a couple important things:</p>
<ul>
<li>What happens if you provide hydration and nutrition to the victim (whether they feel like it or not, such as by feeding tube and IV),</li>
<li>How does the -A reach the victim if they're separated? Do they phase through walls? Teleport? Has the Foundation tried shooting one into space or putting it into some super-duper containment device to see if that stops the process?</li>
<li>How resilient is -B? The Foundation doesn't usually let itself be bullied by SCPs, and I can see them trying out various munitions or other coercive tactics (like threatening to prevent anyone from entering until it complies, threatening to harm/confiscate the animals, etc.)</li>
</ul>
<p>Those are probably my most &quot;Wait&#8230; What?&quot; questions, and they're big enough holes that that I can't justify an upvote until they're addressed in some fashion.</p>

