				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hode" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1570691); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1570691&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607805681" alt="Hode" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1570691)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hode" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1570691); return false;" >Hode</a></span> <span class="odate time_1447914909 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Nov 2015 06:35</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2410153">
									

<p>I feel like the concept is good, but the execution and characters are were this SCP falls flat. For instance, if they know they cannot leave in some circumstances without someone accepting a 2279-a, why would they not bring a D-class with them, and risk two agents lives? Additionally Timmons and Fredericks dialogue feels a bit lazy, it seems more like the dialogue you would see on a buddy cop detective show than a cold and clinical interview. I could understand <em>maybe</em> on the side of Timmons, but I still feel like they would have plenty of training in how to handle a situation like this, or at least know to keep completely quiet and allow the lead agent to do the talking. If this agent was so inexperienced, I don't believe they would have been brought on to any humanoid containment site, no matter the object class.</p>
<p>And a note on your formatting, you should probably remove the first footnote. If I understand what you were saying correctly, then adding a note saying non-human observation methods of the anomaly do not trigger what humans being present will trigger is just redundancy. Like saying, &quot;while humans are not in x, z does not occur, this also does not trigger due to cameras within x.&quot; Well it shouldn't, because a camera is not a human. I would instead suggest removing the footnote.</p>
<p>If you can improve this article, I will change my vote, until then down vote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
